    {
      "id": 93441,
      "name": "HeroComplex",
      "username": "HeroComplex",
      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/h/bbce88/{size}.png",
      "created_at": "2014-03-03T23:11:48.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>You can come up with thematic explanations for it.&nbsp; Combat Stance is about Wraith having trained herself to be extraordinarily alert---but when she's infected, she's weakened, so maybe staying that vigilant actually puts an extra strain on her body.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>For Flame Barrier, maybe when Ra's infected he starts having trouble controlling the fire around him.&nbsp; He's keeping that barrier up all the time, but when the infection kicks in he gets dizzy, loses his focus, and burns himself.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>You've gotta go a little bit afield from what the effects are normally signifying, but I think you can still keep things interesting and flavorful.</p>",
      "post_number": 7,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:19:39.987Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
